      "title": "Upflow velocity sets the cut size",
      "description": "Coarse hydrate crystals settle faster than the rising liquor and report to the underflow as product (to filtration and calcination). Fine crystals are carried up with the overflow and returned to precipitation as seed. The cut size is set by the overflow rate per unit area (upflow velocity) and slurry density — the key to controlling product particle size.",
